# Witness c6_expr_type_selects -- f(1 + tick()) with f(int: a) and f(u8: a): the int pair, seen 1, r 4 (no rule
# that an operator gives an int is used: the numeric contract of integers is open with the author)
# Norm: fable R102/R103; step C6 (PLAN §17)
# Green today, on today's admission (fable Р129, 2026-11-22): 1 + tick() is class (b), a primitive of no known
# type; the pair f(u8: a) is refused before the evaluation because today's admission fills no u8 formal with any
# value (select_operator_u8), so the int pair alone remains: seen 1, r 4. The reason changes: the static type of an
# expression comes with step 21.14, the admission with step 21.8 (a).
(
    Observed:
        int: seen 0
        int: r 0
)
@: shared data[0]
fn: tick () int
    shared\Observed\seen := shared\Observed\seen + 1
    return: 3
fn: f (int: a) int
    shared\Observed\r := a
    return: a
fn: f (u8: a) int
    return: 2
sub: main ()
    f(1 + tick())
main()
